<title>ITALY: Fiat's Magneti buys Portuguese firm.</title>
<headline>Fiat's Magneti buys Portuguese firm.</headline>
<dateline>MILAN 1996-10-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Italian auto components group Magneti Marelli, part of the Fiat group, said it has taken a controlling 59.7 percent stake in Portuguese engine cooling systems manufacturer Joao de Deus Filhos SA.</p>
<p>Magneti said the purchase, for which it gave no financial details, was part of its stategy of expanding its vehicle thermal systems business.</p>
<p>It said in a statement that the Portuguese company produces some 250,000 heat exchangers a year and has a turnover of the equivalent of 17 billion lire.</p>
<p>-- Milan newsroom +392 66129589</p>
</text>
